' 4+1 logical view - States of an outbox message (D-OUTBOX) · OutboxMessage
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever writes the code.
' Documented decision: The email is saved in the outbox in the requester's transaction and sent later, with retries (ADR 0004).
' Not drawn: controllers, HTTP and screens.
@startuml logical-state-outbox
!include ../style.puml
title Logical view - states of an outbox message: OutboxMessage

hide empty description
state Pending : IsPending\nSentAt, FailedAt and SkippedAt empty\ndue when NextAttemptAt ≤ now
state Sent : SentAt
state Skipped : SkippedAt\nnot a failure
state Failed : FailedAt\nnever tried again

[*] --> Pending : OutboxMessage.Create(type, payload, now, dueAt?)\nin the transaction of the change (BookingEmailOutbox, PasswordResetStore)
Pending --> Sent : MarkSent(now)\nIEmailSender.SendAsync succeeded
Pending --> Pending : RecordFailure(error, now, retry) → false\n[Attempts < MaxAttempts]\nNextAttemptAt = now + DelayAfter(Attempts)
Pending --> Failed : RecordFailure(…) → true\n[Attempts ≥ MaxAttempts]
Pending --> Failed : GiveUp(error, now)\nno recipient (recipient_not_found)\nor error reading/composing
Pending --> Skipped : Skip(reason, now)\nreminder: booking_not_confirmed, booking_started\nowner notice: owner_deactivated
Sent --> [*]
Skipped --> [*]
Failed --> [*]

note bottom of Pending
  Only OutboxProcessor.ProcessDueAsync changes the state
  (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, one transaction per batch).
  ck_outbox_messages_one_outcome: at most one of
  sent_at, failed_at, skipped_at. «At least once» delivery.
end note

@enduml
